 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3l-2.5-3z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"13\" r=\"3\"/></svg><span>Enter Photobooth</span></a><a href=\"/studio\" class=\"drawer-cta-secondary\" aria-label=\"Explore Studio\"><svg class=\"cta-grid-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:18px;height:18px;vertical-align:-.15em;display:inline-block;flex-shrink:0\"><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"14\" y=\"3\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"14\" y=\"14\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"3\" y=\"14\" rx=\"1\"/></svg><span>Explore Studio</span></a></div><div class=\"mobile-menu-footer\"><span class=\"mobile-menu-footer-brand\">ConstBooth<br><span style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:normal\">One frame. Beyond distance.</span></span><span class=\"mobile-menu-footer-version\">v2.0.0</span></div></nav><header class=\"main-header full-header\"><div class=\"header-left\"><a href=\"/\" id=\"logo-trigger-top\" class=\"app-logo\" aria-label=\"ConstBooth\"><img src=\"/assets/logo.svg?v=35ddb567\" alt=\"ConstBooth\" class=\"logo-img\" width=\"134\" height=\"36\"></a></div><nav class=\"header-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/#booth-types\">Booths</a> <a href=\"/studio\">Studio</a> <a href=\"/#how\">How it works</a> <a href=\"/blog\">Blog</a> <a href=\"/contact\">Contact</a></nav><div class=\"header-actions\"><a href=\"/booth\" class=\"nav-cta\"><svg class=\"cta-icon-camera\" aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:1.18em;height:1.18em;vertical-align:-.18em;margin-right:7px;display:inline-block;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M14.5 4h-5L7 7H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3l-2.5-3z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"13\" r=\"3\"/></svg><span>Enter Photobooth</span></a></div></header><main id=\"main-content\"><div class=\"blog-page-wrap\"><div class=\"blog-container\"></div><section class=\"blog-hero\"><nav class=\"blog-eyebrow reveal\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\" class=\"blog-eyebrow-link\">Home</a><span class=\"blog-crumb-sep\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&middot;</span><a href=\"/blog\" class=\"blog-eyebrow-link\">Blog</a><span class=\"blog-crumb-sep\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&middot;</span><a href=\"/blog/category/studio\" class=\"blog-eyebrow-link\">Studio</a></nav><h1 class=\"reveal delay-1\">How to Make a <span class=\"accent\">Digital Cassette</span> With Your Voice, Photos & Memories</h1><p class=\"blog-hero-sub reveal delay-2\">A voice note is a recording. A digital cassette is a recording someone actually opens - here’s how to make one.</p><div class=\"blog-meta reveal delay-3\"><div class=\"blog-meta-author\"><div class=\"blog-meta-avatar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7\" r=\"4\"/></svg></div><span class=\"blog-meta-name\"><a href=\"/about#author\">Kishan Naik</a></span></div><span class=\"blog-meta-date\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:14px;height:14px;opacity:.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> <time datetime=\"2026-09-18\">September 18, 2026</time> </span><span class=\"blog-meta-read\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:14px;height:14px;opacity:.5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 7 min read</span></div></section><div class=\"blog-container\"><aside class=\"lb-rail lb-rail--blog lb-rail--follow lb-rail--l\" data-rail=\"blog\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><div class=\"lb-rail-ad\"></div></aside><aside class=\"lb-rail lb-rail--blog lb-rail--follow lb-rail--r\" data-rail=\"blog\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><div class=\"lb-rail-ad\"></div></aside>\n<figure class=\"blog-cover reveal\"><picture><source type=\"image/avif\" srcset=\"/assets/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message-960.avif?v=b3c336dc 960w, /assets/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message-1920.avif?v=92c988fe 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/assets/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message-960.webp?v=37a1978f 960w, /assets/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message-1920.webp?v=2e9dede4 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px\"><img src=\"/assets/blog/digital-cassette-voice-message-960.webp?v=37a1978f\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Two cassette tapes labelled Awesome Mix, one pink and one yellow\" loading=\"eager\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\"></picture></figure><article class=\"blog-body\" id=\"blog-article\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/BlogPosting\"><nav class=\"blog-toc reveal\" aria-labelledby=\"toc-heading\"><h2 id=\"toc-heading\" class=\"blog-toc-title\">In this article</h2><ol class=\"blog-toc-list\"><li><a href=\"#s1\">What is a digital cassette?</a></li><li><a href=\"#s2\">What can you put on a digital cassette?</a></li><li><a href=\"#s3\">How to create a digital cassette in ConstBooth</a></li><li><a href=\"#s4\">Digital cassette ideas</a></li><li><a href=\"#s5\">Why add a photo to a voice message?</a></li><li><a href=\"#s6\">If your message doesn't have one recipient</a></li><li><a href=\"#faq\">Frequently Asked Questions</a></li></ol></nav>\n<section class=\"blog-section\"><p class=\"reveal\">A voice note is a recording. A digital cassette is a recording someone opens on purpose. The audio can be identical - what changes is everything around it: a cover you designed, a label with a photo and a date on it, and a small ritual on the other end before the voice actually plays. That's what turns a thirty-second clip into something worth keeping.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Here's what a digital cassette actually is, what you can put on one, and how to make one in ConstBooth.</p></section>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s1\"><h2 id=\"s1\" class=\"reveal\">What is a digital cassette?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">It's a voice recording wrapped in the format of a cassette tape rather than a bare audio file. Three things separate it from the alternatives:</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\"><strong>Versus a normal voice note.</strong> A voice note is one tap and gone - no cover, no context, easy to lose in a chat thread. A cassette has a cover you customize and a label with a photo and text, so it looks like something rather than just sounding like something.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\"><strong>Versus a static photo.</strong> A photo freezes a moment but says nothing in your own voice. A cassette does the opposite - it's built around the voice, with the photo as a supporting element rather than the whole thing.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\"><strong>Versus a generic audio recorder.</strong> A plain recording app gives you a file. A cassette gives the person receiving it a small physical-feeling moment - they watch it slide into a player before it starts, rather than just pressing play on a waveform.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">None of this changes what a recording actually is technically. What changes is the presentation, and presentation is most of what makes something feel worth keeping rather than worth deleting once it's been heard.</p></section>\n\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s2\"><h2 id=\"s2\" class=\"reveal\">What can you put on a digital cassette?</h2><ul class=\"blog-list reveal delay-1\"><li><strong>Your voice.</strong> The core of it - an actual recording, not typed text read aloud by anything else.</li><li><strong>One photo.</strong> Cropped, repositioned and zoomed until it sits right on the label.</li><li><strong>Short text.</strong> A line or two - a title, a name, a note.</li><li><strong>An optional date.</strong> When it was made, or a date that matters to what you're saying.</li><li><strong>A cover and label design.</strong> Customize how the cassette itself looks before anything else goes on it.</li></ul></section>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s3\"><h2 id=\"s3\" class=\"reveal\">How to create a digital cassette in ConstBooth</h2><ol class=\"blog-list reveal delay-1\"><li><strong>Open Cassette Studio.</strong> Go to <a href=\"/studio/cassette\" class=\"inline-link\">ConstBooth Cassette</a> to start.</li><li><strong>Choose and customize a design.</strong> Pick a cassette style and adjust the cover and label.</li><li><strong>Add your photo.</strong> Crop, reposition and zoom it until it fits the label.</li><li><strong>Add text and a date, if you want them.</strong> Both are optional.</li><li><strong>Record your voice.</strong> Start recording whenever you're ready.</li><li><strong>Preview it.</strong> Listen back before deciding it's done.</li><li><strong>Re-record if it's not right.</strong> No limit on doing it again until it sounds how you want.</li><li><strong>Broadcast or share it.</strong> Send it once you're happy with it.</li><li><strong>The receiver plays the cassette.</strong> They watch it slide into a player, then press play to hear you.</li></ol><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Nothing about the process needs an account, and it runs in the browser on desktop or mobile.</p></section>\n\n\n\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s4\"><h2 id=\"s4\" class=\"reveal\">Digital cassette ideas</h2><ul class=\"blog-list reveal delay-1\"><li><strong>Birthday voice message.</strong> Says more than a written message, and takes about the same effort.</li><li><strong>Long-distance message.</strong> For when a text feels too flat for what you actually want to say.</li><li><strong>Travel memory.</strong> Record while somewhere, or talk about it afterward - both work, and the photo can be from either moment.</li><li><strong>Friendship message.</strong> Not everything has to be romantic; a cassette for a friend works exactly the same way.</li><li><strong>A personal story.</strong> Something you'd rather tell than type - longer stories tend to survive better as voice than as a wall of text.</li><li><strong>An audio-memory snippet.</strong> A short recollection of one specific moment, kept exactly as it sounded when you first said it out loud.</li></ul><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">If you plan to include a song or melody, make sure you actually hold the rights to it or that it's genuinely yours to share - ConstBooth doesn't grant any license to use someone else's music.</p></section>\n\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s5\"><h2 id=\"s5\" class=\"reveal\">Why add a photo to a voice message?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A recording on its own has no anchor - months later, it's not always obvious what the voice was even talking about. A photo pins it to a specific moment, the same way a caption pins a picture. Put the two together and each one fills in what the other is missing: the photo shows what things looked like, the voice explains what it felt like at the time.</p><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">It also changes how the recording gets received. A voice note that arrives with no context asks the listener to guess what they're about to hear. A cassette with a photo and a date already tells them roughly what it is before they press play - they're choosing to listen, not being ambushed by an unlabeled file.</p></section>\n<aside class=\"blog-inline-cta reveal\" aria-label=\"Try ConstBooth Cassette\"><p class=\"blog-inline-cta-text\">Free, no account needed. Record, preview, and re-record as many times as you like.</p><a class=\"blog-inline-cta-btn\" href=\"/studio/cassette\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"width:1.1em;height:1.1em;vertical-align:-.15em;margin-right:6px;display:inline-block\"><path d=\"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/></svg>Make a Cassette</a></aside>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"s6\"><h2 id=\"s6\" class=\"reveal\">If your message doesn't have one recipient</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A cassette is built for a specific person. If what you actually want is to hear a voice that isn't addressed to you at all - or leave one for a stranger rather than someone you know - <a href=\"/blog/anonymous-voice-messages-tiny-radio\" class=\"inline-link\">ConstBooth Radio</a> is the format built for that instead.</p></section>\n<section class=\"blog-section\" aria-labelledby=\"faq\"><h2 id=\"faq\" class=\"reveal\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">What is a digital cassette?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A voice recording presented as a customizable cassette tape, with your own photo and short text on the label, that the recipient opens like a physical cassette before it plays.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">Can I record my own voice on a digital cassette?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Yes, that’s the core of it - you record, preview, and can re-record as many times as you want before sending.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">Can I add a photo to a digital cassette?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">Yes, one photo, which you can crop, reposition and zoom to fit the label.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:24px\"><h2 class=\"reveal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12px\">How is a digital cassette different from a normal voice message?</h2><p class=\"reveal delay-1\">A normal voice message is a bare recording. A cassette wraps the same recording in a cover and label you design, with a photo and text, and the receiver watches it load into a player before it plays.</p></div></section>\n<div class=\"blog-tag-row\" aria-label=\"Article tags\"><span class=\"blog-tag-label\">Filed under</span><a class=\"blog-tag-chip\" href=\"/blog/tag/nostalgia\" rel=\"tag\">Nostalgia</a></div><section class=\"blog-related\" aria-labelledby=\"related-heading\"><h2 id=\"related-heading\" class=\"blog-related-title\">Keep reading</h2><div class=\"blog-related-grid\"><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/creative-ways-to-make-digital-memories-online\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Studio</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">3 Creative Ways to Make Digital Memories Online</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">Letters, cassettes and ConstBooth Radio - three formats, and which one fits what you’re after.</span></a><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/anonymous-voice-messages-tiny-radio\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Studio</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">ConstBooth Radio: Hear Anonymous Voice Messages From Strangers Online</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">When the voice you want to hear - or send - doesn’t belong to someone you know.</span></a><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/digital-love-letter-online\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Studio</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">How to Make a Digital Love Letter Online With Photos &amp; Memories</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">When a written page says it better than a recording.</span></a><a class=\"blog-related-card\" href=\"/blog/the-comeback-of-photo-strips\"><span class=\"blog-related-cat\">Culture</span><span class=\"blog-related-h\">The Comeback of Photo Strips</span><span class=\"blog-related-p\">Why an old format keeps returning, and what that says about what people actually want to keep.</span></a></div></section><div style=\"margin-top:48px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/blog\" class=\"inline-link\" style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:600\">&larr; Back to blog</a></div>\n\n</article></div></div></main><footer class=\"site-footer\"><div class=\"footer-main\"><div class=\"footer-brand\"><div class=\"footer-logo\"><a href=\"/\" aria-label=\"ConstBooth\"><img src=\"/assets/logo-footer.svg?v=b1cb43c4\" alt=\"ConstBooth\" class=\"footer-logo-img\" width=\"134\" height=\"36\"></a></div><p class=\"footer-tagline\">One frame. Beyond distance.</p><div class=\"footer-socials\"><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/app.lensbooth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"footer-social-link\" aria-label=\"Instagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"2\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"17.5\" cy=\"6.5\" r=\"1\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/></svg> </a><a href=\"https://x.com/lensboothapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"footer-social-link\" aria-label=\"X (Twitter)\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z\"/></svg></a><a href=\"https://in.pinterest.com/lensboothapp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"footer-social-link\" aria-label=\"Pinterest\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.or